# Documentation Instructions

## Scope

These rules apply under `docs/`. Documentation describes the implementation that exists now; plans and temporary investigation state belong elsewhere.

## Ownership

- Put component and interface relationships in [architecture.md](architecture.md).
- Put environment and canonical commands in [development.md](development.md).
- Put validation entry-point status and result interpretation in [testing.md](testing.md).
- {{CONDITIONAL_DOC_OWNERS}}

Do not duplicate a fact owned elsewhere. Link its owner.

## Writing

- Prefer direct current-state prose.
- Separate established facts from unknowns.
- Keep examples executable or label them illustrative.
- Update links and owners in the same change.
- Do not include editing-session narration, review dialogue, or hidden reasoning.
